  "decision": "Keep: reusing decoded branch vectors saves 99,998 execution allocations and 799,872 allocated bytes per 100,000 statement or expression if iterations on macOS. Mac timing improves by 1.8 ms for statement if and 4.8 ms for expression if; the inline loop control is flat. Pinned Linux timing is near flat at 100,000 and 500,000 iterations, with control drift of similar size. RSS on both hosts is slightly higher, including the control, and does not establish a pool memory benefit. macOS filtered runtime passed 199 tests with 17 ignored, runner lib passed 20, native basic passed 9 with one skipped, and native frontend-indexed passed 3; pinned Linux passed 205 with 17 ignored, 20 runner tests, 9 basic with one skipped, and 3 frontend-indexed."
